    "intake_questions_67EfND": {
      "type": "intake-questions",
      "blocks": {
        "question_8XTRQG": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "... use hormonal contraceptives?",
            "answer": "<p>You can take monthlies while on birth control or hormonal contraceptive pills;<br/>however, it’s essential to understand that the effectiveness of monthlies may<br/>vary since your hormones are already being regulated. Additionally, monthlies<br/>could potentially interact with your hormonal birth control. To ensure safety,<br/>it’s always best to consult your doctor before adding any new supplements to<br/>your routine.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_MHBmhx": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "... am undergoing fertility treatment?",
            "answer": "<p>Fertility treatments often require precise hormonal adjustments.<br/>Please make sure to only take any new supplements, including monthlies, in consultation with your doctor. External supplements may interfere with the intended hormonal changes of your treatment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_UHThCX": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "... am taking other supplements?",
            "answer": "<p>It really depends on which other supplements you’re taking and for what reason. Good additions to monthlies can include omega-3 fatty acids, probiotics, or evening primrose oil - depending on your personal needs. Please check with your doctor, or reach out to us in the chat if you’d like more guidance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_i4dEtW": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "... am trying to conceive?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, you can take monthlies while you’re trying to conceive. While it isn’t a prenatal supplement, it does include the recommended daily amount of folate for women of childbearing age (400 mcg).  However, it’s important to stop taking monthlies as soon as you find out you’re pregnant.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_mnYNP6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "... have PCOS",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have PCOS, as there are many ingredients that may benefit those with PCOS. However, monthlies is not meant to treat any medical condition so you should always check with your doctor before incorporating new supplements into your routine. Please also check for possible interactions with your medications (if any).</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_qPY3xK": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "... have endometriosis?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have endometriosis. While monthlies is not a treatment for endometriosis, it’s designed to support menstrual well-being by addressing some of the underlying triggers of period pain, such as hormonal imbalances, prostaglandin overproduction, and nutrient gaps. </p><p>However, we always recommend you to check with your doctor before adding any new supplements to your routine, and check for possible interactions with medications.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_ki4qdy": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "... am pregnant or breastfeeding?",
            "answer": "<p>It isn’t recommended to take monthlies while pregnant or breastfeeding, as not all ingredients are considered safe during pregnancy or lactation.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "question_8XTRQG",
        "question_MHBmhx",
